description:
Why this choice is correct: pkix-aia/src/lib.rs:664-668 contains:

const _: fn() = || {
    fn _assert_send_sync<T: Send + Sync>() {}
    _assert_send_sync::<AiaError>();
    _assert_send_sync::<NoAiaFetcher>();
};

This compile-time assertion catches any future field addition that would break the Send+Sync invariant — a raw pointer, an Rc<T>, a non-Send handle. It costs zero at runtime, costs nothing in the public surface (the const _ is private), and fails fast at the build that introduces the regression rather than at a downstream consumer's load-test.

A future contributor might suggest removing it ('Send+Sync is auto-derived; this is redundant'). Reject: the assertion is precisely for the case where a future field SILENTLY breaks the auto-derive. The const _ trick is the workspace-standard pattern (per memory send-sync-invariant-in-pkix-workspace-pkix-2l0v); it should be preserved here and mirrored in every result/error type the workspace ships.
